<figure><img src="https://baty.net/img/2026/20260811-vaer-watch.webp" alt="VAER C5 Tactical Solar"></figure><p>I had to buy a new watch so that I would stop wanting more watches. I know it's counter-intuitive, but hear me out.</p>
<!-- more -->
<p>I like watches. It started after I bought a nice Tag Heuer automatic to reward myself for some achievement (which I've forgotten). It's a nice watch. Expensive. It's fifteen years old and I've never wound it or replaced a battery. This was my window into automatic watches.</p>
<p>Then came the Apple Watch, which I wore for years, dutifully upgrading every couple of years. I grew to dislike it. It's too needy.</p>
<p>Then I rebelled and started buying cheap watches instead. First it was a little Casio F91W for like $20. Then I upgraded to a few different G-Shocks. It turned out that out of all of them, the G-Shock GWM5610 was the one I always wore.</p>
<p><img src="https://baty.net/img/2026/20260811-casio.webp" alt="Casio watch" /></p>
<p>My recent attempts to &quot;Reduce &amp; Simplify&quot; have been somewhat successful, so I wanted to do it with my watches. I didn't have <em>that</em> many, but still.</p>
<p>I get a kick out of wearing cheap watches, so I haven't been wearing the Tag except for &quot;nicer&quot; things like going out to dinner. Even then it bugged me, so I decided to find something simple, decent looking, and less expensive than the Tag for wearing out.</p>
<p>I landed on a <a href="https://www.vaerwatches.com/products/c5-tactical-field-40mm-usa-solar">VAER C5 Tactical Field Solar</a>.</p>
<p><img src="https://baty.net/img/2026/20260811-vaer-watch.webp" alt="VAER watch" /></p>
<p>I think it's great. Large, easy to read numbers (with 24-hour times, too) that glow brightly in the dark. It's solar, so never needs winding. It has a screw-down crown, so it's &quot;ocean proof&quot;. Sapphire glass so it's at least somewhat scratch-resistent. It came with two bands. One silicon for normal wear and one nylon one for a nicer look. I dig it. It cost $349.</p>
<p>Anyway, I now only wear either the G-Shock or the VAER. They cover every occasion. See? I bought something so I could stop buying things. I think it'll work</p>
